WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
In 2023, a new treatment for sickle cell
disease was approved in the UK and the

2
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:06.800
USA.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.260
It edits DNA in a patient's
own blood-forming stem cells.

4
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:17.930
In the trial, 29 of 30 patients had no
severe pain crises for at least a year.

5
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.260
So how do scientists work
out what a gene does,

6
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.640
and how can they rewrite one?

7
00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:28.920
In this mission, you'll see how a guide
RNA of about 20 bases leads the enzyme

8
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:32.040
Cas9 to one exact place.

9
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:37.290
Then you'll weigh the ethics: why editing
an embryo raises questions that editing

10
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.630
one patient's cells does not.

11
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.720
Your mission: find out how
scientists learn what a gene does,

12
00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.830
and rewrite it.
